# ARK Mobile Projection

ARK Mobile is a **mobile projection**, not a separate product.

## Lock

- Authority stays in ARK V2 (MySQL, Laravel, existing domains)
- Mobile consumes `/api/mobile/*` — never scrapes Blade
- **Sanctum** bearer auth — no Firebase Auth, no mobile-only users
- **Spatie permissions** — Flutter never decides authority
- Findings create existing **`InspectionItem`** — no parallel Finding store
- Communications consume **`Conversation`** + **`UnifiedOperationalTimeline`** — no SMS inbox authority
- **Comms transport lock:** SMS/MMS and conversation timeline never use provider SDKs — only `/api/mobile/communications*`. See `docs/mobile/ark-mobile-communications-authority-contract.md`
- **ARK Phone exception:** Voice dialer (`ArkVoiceDialer`, `sip_ua`, optional `twilio_voice`) is a **first-class SIP endpoint** — not a messaging transport. Must follow [ark-phone-mission.mdc](ark-phone-mission.mdc) and [ark-phone-production-telephony-lock.mdc](ark-phone-production-telephony-lock.mdc); research before inventing.
- **Notification lock:** ARK owns notification authority; APNs/FCM transport only — no Firebase Auth, Firestore, or Firebase-driven workflow. Push **deferred** until floor observation. See `docs/mobile/ark-mobile-notification-doctrine.md`

## API naming

Use `/api/mobile/{resource}` — not `/api/flutter`, `/api/tech`, or versioned mobile silos.

## Technician scope

Assigned RO discovery only unless user has `operations.access`.

Comms on mobile for technicians = conversations linked to **assigned** ROs.

## Flutter (separate repo)

- Phone-first; not a desktop clone
- `flutter_secure_storage` for tokens
- Riverpod for state
- Photo capture → upload to ARK → attachment id returned

